+# Changes
+
+## Round 1
+
+Implemented `compare(a, b)` in `src/semver.mjs`:
+
+- **Parsing/validation**: added a `parse()` helper that validates each argument
+  is a `string` (else `TypeError`) and matches the canonical semver.org regular
+  expression for a valid SemVer 2.0.0 string (else `RangeError`). The regex
+  enforces: numeric major/minor/patch with no leading zeros; pre-release
+  identifiers that are either all-digit with no leading zero, or alphanumeric
+  (leading zeros allowed there); build metadata identifiers (alphanumeric,
+  leading zeros allowed); no trailing/leading whitespace or extra segments.
+- **Precedence (§11)**: compares major, minor, patch numerically first. If
+  those are equal, compares pre-release fields:
+  - a version without a pre-release has higher precedence than one with a
+    pre-release, given equal major/minor/patch;
+  - pre-release identifiers are split on `.` and compared left to right;
+  - purely numeric identifiers compare numerically; identifiers that aren't
+    purely numeric compare as strings (ASCII order); numeric identifiers
+    always have lower precedence than non-numeric ones;
+  - if all shared identifiers are equal, the pre-release with more fields has
+    higher precedence.
+  - build metadata (`+…`) is parsed and discarded — it never affects
+    precedence.
+
+No tests were changed. `tests/semver.test.mjs` was used as-is to drive the
+implementation; no new test file was added because the existing suite already
+exercises numeric/alphanumeric comparisons, the full §11 example chain,
+leading-zero edge cases, build-metadata handling, invalid-string rejection,
+and non-string rejection — the specification's own words say these tests
+represent the spec.
+
+### Test results
+
+`npm test` → 10/10 suites passing (0 failing):
+
+- major, minor and patch compare as numbers
+- equal versions compare as 0
+- a pre-release comes before its release
+- pre-release identifiers follow the §11 chain
+- numeric identifiers compare as numbers, and rank below alphanumeric ones
+- build metadata does not count
+- sorting with compare orders a mixed list
+- a string that is not a semantic version throws a RangeError
+- a leading zero is allowed in build metadata and in alphanumeric identifiers
+- an argument that is not a string throws a TypeError
